<!-- 6. 3DGS 训练评估 (Point 7, 8, 9, 10 + SOR Ablation) -->
<div id="3dgs-eval">
  <h3>Phase III: 3DGS Rendering Fidelity & The PSNR Trap</h3>
  
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
      <img src="https://placehold.co/600x350?text=Training+Convergence+Chart" class="img-fluid rounded">
      <p class="mt-2"><small>3DGS Training Evolution: 7k (Structure) vs 50k (Fidelity)</small></p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
      <h5>The "Sweet Spot" Discovery</h5>
      <p>While PSNR peaks at <strong>50,000 iterations</strong> (up to 44.29 dB), we identify <strong>7,000 iterations</strong> as the "Visual Sweet Spot." Beyond 21k, model risks <strong>anisotropic collapse</strong> (Gaussians becoming too flat), fitting pixels but sacrificing novel view consistency.</p>
      
      <h5>Ablation: Impact of SOR Denoising</h5>
      <p>SOR refinement (removing 7.3% outliers) provides a <strong>+0.41 dB</strong> PSNR gain early (7k iter) and completely eliminates unphysical "floaters," ensuring a cleaner navigable scene.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

